      "title": "Line segments: LSD vs Hough vs FLD vs Edge Drawing",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "LSD (cv2.createLineSegmentDetector) against the classic Hough pipeline.\n\nLSD is a cv2 CLASS rather than a plain function, so it comes as the curated 'CV Detect Line Segments (LSD)' node instead of a raw cv2.* wrapper: the node creates the detector, uses it and drops it in one run, so no live handle crosses the graph.\n\nRow 1 - LSD works on the GRADIENT FIELD directly: no Canny step, no accumulator resolution, no threshold to tune. Every segment has subpixel endpoints, a measured WIDTH and (in 'advanced' mode) an NFA confidence.\nRow 2 - the same image through cv2.Canny + cv2.HoughLinesP for comparison. Hough votes for infinite lines and then cuts them, so it happily fuses two collinear edges into one segment and needs three thresholds to behave.\nRow 3 - the same LSD run with min_length, which is what turns a cluttered result into the structural edges only.\n\nRows 4-5 - FLD (cv2.ximgproc.createFastLineDetector), the third family: Canny, then chain the edge pixels and cut each chain where it stops being straight. It is the fastest of the three, it has a real length threshold inside the detector, and do_merge glues collinear neighbours back together - the one thing LSD will not do. Row 5 is the same node with canny_aperture_size = 0, which skips the internal Canny and takes the edge map from row 2 as its input, so ANY edge node in the pack can drive it.\n\nRows 6-8 - Edge Drawing (cv2.ximgproc.createEdgeDrawing) does not threshold a gradient at all: it seeds ANCHORS at gradient maxima and walks the ridge between them, so the edge map is one pixel wide and already CHAINED. The chains come out as CV_CONTOURS (row 7, drawn with 'CV Draw Contours' - every contour node in the pack accepts them), and the straight fits come out in the same Nx4 layout as Hough / LSD / FLD (row 8).\n\nRow 9 - EDCircles, the part no other line detector here has: the same chains fitted as CIRCLES and ELLIPSES. A dial seen at an angle comes back as an ellipse with its own angle, not as a circle.\n\nTHE SHEET (right-hand column) - every row's overlay goes into ONE 'CreateList', so 'Draw Text' and 'Preview CV Array' each execute once per tile and all nine results land in a SINGLE preview, captioned. The captions are one ';'-separated string split by 'Basic data handling: RegexSplitDataList', so they stay in CreateList order - reorder the list and reorder the string with it. The Edge Drawing edge map is a single-channel array, so it passes through 'Preview CV Array' first to become an IMAGE like the other tiles.\n\nTry: set refine to 'advanced (NFA validated)' and watch the count drop to the segments the false-alarm test accepts; raise min_length until only the poster borders survive; turn do_merge off in row 4 and count the pieces one poster border breaks into; or raise Edge Drawing's gradient_threshold and watch the low-contrast chains go."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
